<h1>ZxBudget Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="muted">Last updated: June 16, 2026</p>

<p>ZxBudget is a personal budgeting app for iPhone, iPad, and Mac. Protecting
your privacy is a core design goal: the app is built so that the developer
never has access to your financial data.</p>

<h2>Data we collect</h2>
<p><strong>None.</strong> The developer of ZxBudget does not collect, receive,
store, sell, or share any of your personal or financial information. There is
no account to create with us, no analytics, no advertising, and no third-party
tracking SDKs in the app.</p>

<h2>Where your data lives</h2>
<p>All of your budget data — accounts, transactions, categories, targets, and
settings — is stored locally on your device and in <strong>your own private
iCloud account</strong> using Apple's CloudKit private database. This data is
synced between your devices by Apple and is governed by
<a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple's Privacy Policy</a>.
The developer cannot see, access, or retrieve it.</p>

<h2>Network usage</h2>
<p>ZxBudget connects to the internet for two purposes only:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>iCloud sync</strong>, handled entirely by Apple, to keep your
  data consistent across your devices.</li>
  <li><strong>Foreign-exchange rates</strong>, fetched from public sources
  (the Bank of Canada and the Frankfurter / European Central Bank rate feeds)
  to convert amounts for multi-currency budgets. These requests ask only for
  public exchange-rate data and contain none of your personal or financial
  information.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Data sharing and budget collaboration</h2>
<p>If you choose to share a budget with another person using the app's built-in
sharing feature, that data is shared directly between your iCloud accounts
through Apple's CloudKit sharing. The developer is not a party to that exchange
and does not receive the shared data.</p>

<h2>Data retention and deletion</h2>
<p>Because the developer holds none of your data, there is nothing for us to
retain or delete. You remain in full control: you can edit or remove data in
the app, reset your budget, export a backup, or delete the app and remove its
data from your iCloud account at any time.</p>

<h2>Children</h2>
<p>ZxBudget is not directed at children and does not knowingly collect any
information from anyone, including children under the age of 13.</p>

<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>If this policy changes, the updated version will be posted on this page with
a new "Last updated" date.</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>
<p>Questions about this policy or the app? Email
<a href="mailto:zxiiro@gmail.com">zxiiro@gmail.com</a>.</p>

